{"statement_verdicts":[{"obj_id":"def:pair-derivations","verdict":"matched","note":"IsPairDerivations is by definition IsCoordEulerDerivation, which realizes the binding pin ass:pin-3. In the Lean, b is an explicit, universally quantified p-basis (Fin e, matching the finite lists of def:p-basis), with s = b j and t = b k at distinct positions, and Ds, Dt are C-linear derivations (C = powSubfield = F^p) taking the coordinate Euler values on b. The paper's condition that the pair is p-independent is not stated separately but follows: two distinct entries of a p-basis form a p-independent sublist (tower law, each adjunction has degree at most p). Conversely, the paper's D_s, D_t from any extending p-basis satisfy the Lean clauses, so the two definitions have the same extension."},{"obj_id":"def:scalar-action","verdict":"matched","note":"The Lean gives a MulAction of (ZMod p)ˣ = Λˣ on the subtype {Θ // IsCompatibleIso p Θ}, acting by pointwise scalar multiplication r • Θ x (scalarAct). The NL's claim that the set is closed under this action is carried by scalarAct_compatible, a proved lemma rather than an assumption, under PrimeChar p (ass:prime, needed for Λ = F_p). The one_smul and mul_smul axioms are the module axioms on V_L. Same object as the NL's scalar action of Λˣ on Isom_M(V_K,V_L)."}],"assumption_verdicts":[{"obj_id":"ass:pin-3","verdict":"faithful-refinement","note":"Unfolded: IsPBasis p F b means [C(b):C] = p^e and C(b) = F, i.e. def:p-basis for a finite list over C = F^p. Then j ≠ k, b j = s and b k = t mean the basis extends the pair s,t; their positions do not matter up to reindexing. Ds and Dt are C-linear derivations F→F with Ds(b_i) = δ_ij·b_j and Dt(b_i) = δ_ik·b_k. Since F = C[b] is algebraic over C, a C-derivation is determined by its values on the generators. By Leibniz these values give D_j(monomial) = i_j·monomial, the coordinate Euler derivation of lem:p-basis, and the converse holds too. b is a free parameter, matching 'one fixed, arbitrarily chosen' basis, and it is not chosen from the conclusion or from consumers. The finite Fin e indexing matches def:p-basis, where a p-basis is a finite list. The two are equivalent."}],"substrate_gates":[],"escalate":null}
